hey David you talk a lot about believing  women but what would you do if you were  falsely accused of sexual assault let's  discuss it this actually came up when I  was on remember that show I went on in  LA  the Jesse Lee Peterson show we were  talking about the Brett Kavanaugh  hearings and he asked me in some way  would you want to be accused of a sexual  assault you didn't commit and I said  that's not really a question Jesse no  one I don't I don't want anyone accused  of a crime that they didn't commit of  course and in fact there was a movement  to do this at a time when I was covering  the Cavanagh hearings I started hearing  from people who said David we're going  to go to your local papers we are going  to claim that you sexually assaulted  someone and my understanding is that  some of those allegations were actually  made and they went nowhere because they  obviously were not credible but let's  answer the question as asked false rape  or sexual assault allegations are very  rare but when they happen they should be  punished and I've said that for a very  long time but let's play it out what  would I do if I were accused of sexual  assault or rape and I had not done  anything wrong  first and foremost I would say nothing  and I would immediately call a lawyer  now I know that that already puts me in  a position of privilege right not  everybody can afford a lawyer well if  the police want to talk to you if you  are being compelled to talk to them then  you can request a lawyer and if you are  not being compelled to talk to them then  I simply would not talk to them but I  would immediately reach out to a lawyer  I would not attempt to contact the  accuser I would not attempt to contact  the accusers family I would immediately  think to myself who might be able to  either provide an alibi or be a witness  in some way I would immediately try to  put in writing whatever interactions I  may have had in my life with the accuser  if there are any if it's genuinely  someone I don't even know I would of  course not have any interactions to  write down but if it is someone that is  known to me I would immediately put in  writing interactions I would check  social media records I would check email  whatever and and really categorize for  myself what the interactions have been  if any now I get it  false allegations anytime  that you have a system that allows  people to make a complaint that they  have been victimized by someone else  there will be some percentage of either  straight-up false allegations or  mistaken identity problems where an  accuser believes it was this person when  in reality it was that person what I I  really want to state here is I'm glad to  answer the question about what I would  do these are not common situations I  don't want to give them more importance  than they deserve I believe it is a far  bigger problem for those who are  victimized by sexual assault or rape to  never have justice done to the  perpetrator that is a far bigger problem  mathematically than false rape  allegations most importantly the most  important thing that I do in order to  avoid allegations of any kind is I don't  sexually harass or assault people which  in 99.99 whatever percent of the cases  is actually your best insurance if I'm  missing something if the actions I would  take are not the right ones let me know  what I'm missing we have a great bonus  show coming up for you today  of course the Friday bonus show hosted  by producer Pat and he will be telling  you about next week's plan with  Thanksgiving upcoming and much much more  so make sure you are a member at join  pakman.com or a patron at patreon.com  slash david pakman show Pat will speak  to you then I'll be back on Monday
 

